Privacy Policy — UtilityHub Pro

Last Updated: August 27, 2026

UtilityHub Pro ("the App") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use UtilityHub Pro.

1. Information We Collect

UtilityHub Pro is designed to work primarily on your device.

The current version does not intentionally collect, sell, or share personal information with us.

The App does not require you to create an account or provide personal information such as your name, email address, phone number, or physical address.

2. Local Data Storage

Some features may store information locally on your device using browser/app storage.

This can include:

- App settings
- Theme preferences
- Favorite tools
- Recently used tools
- Notes created inside the App

This information is stored locally on your device and is not intentionally transmitted to our servers by the current version of the App.

If you uninstall the App or clear its app data, locally stored information may be deleted.

3. Images and Files

If you use image-related tools, selected images or files are processed on your device where supported.

UtilityHub Pro does not intentionally upload your selected images or files to our servers in the current version.

4. Camera and Device Features

If a future feature requires access to a device function such as the camera, the App will request the appropriate permission when necessary.

Permissions are used only for the functionality that requires them.

5. Advertising

UtilityHub Pro currently contains no advertisements.

The current version does not intentionally use advertising SDKs or display third-party advertisements.

If advertising is introduced in a future version, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.

6. Analytics and Tracking

The current version of UtilityHub Pro does not intentionally use third-party analytics or advertising tracking services.

We do not intentionally create advertising profiles based on your activity inside the App.

7. Third-Party Services

The current version is designed to provide its core functionality without requiring third-party online services for normal use.

If third-party services are introduced in future versions, this Privacy Policy will be updated to explain their use.

8. Children's Privacy

UtilityHub Pro does not intentionally collect personal information from children or other users.

Because the App does not require an account for normal use, users can access its basic functionality without providing personal information.

9. Data Security

We aim to keep the App's locally stored information protected through the security mechanisms provided by the user's device and operating system.

However, no digital storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy when the App's features, data practices, or services change.

Any updated version will include a new "Last Updated" date.

11. Contact Us

If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or UtilityHub Pro, please contact the developer through the contact information provided on the App's Google Play Store listing.

